Error case: --to is before --from, so the exit code is 2 (usage) before any request.
-- args --
activity
trim
12345678
--from
10m
--to
5m
-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
Usage: gccli activity trim <id> [flags]

Trim the start or end of an activity.

For single-sport activities and the legs of a multisport activity. Give --from,
--to or both. Garmin applies the trim in a few seconds. To bring back the
original, use activity restore.

Arguments:
  <id>    Activity ID.

Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json              Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain             Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header            Print the column names as the first line of --plain
                          output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"      Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING    Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"      Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                          elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                          auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us, statute_uk
                          ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version           Print version information.

      --from=FROM         New start, as the time since the activity start (e.g.
                          2m, 1h5m). Default: the activity start.
      --to=TO             New end, as the time since the activity start (e.g.
                          50m, 1h5m). Default: the activity end.

gccli: error: activity trim: --to 5m0s is not after --from 10m0s
